2.2 Ruled out by reading
• SQL injection - the solution contains no SQL.
• XML external entities - XmlHelper.TryParseXmlSeguro sets XmlResolver = null (XmlHelper.cs:23); the only other XML construction uses XElement (escaped) or the unescaped templates covered by CHR-FR-14.
• Undisposed crypto - both TripleDESCryptoServiceProvider uses are inside using blocks (RSAUtilEncrypt.cs:52, 80).
• `throw ex;` / sync-over-async in the request path - none; the single GetAwaiter().GetResult() (ServiceHost.cs:560) is inside the synchronous OnStop override.
• Overlapping ticks / timers - there is no timer; requests are driven by the TCP listener.
• Unguarded nullable dereferences in the request path - the only .Value calls are the two Pid.Value uses in start-up (CHR-FR-29); the EF-style FirstOrDefault() pattern does not occur.
3. What's Already Good
• Layering and interfaces. Application / infrastructure split with an interface for every RSA/HSM collaborator (IRSAAdminService, IRSATokenService, IHsmClient, IRSASoapClient, ...) and constructor injection throughout - the shape the baseline (4.3) asks for, and the reason the missing tests in CHR-FR-31 are cheap to add.
• DI composition is verified at start-up. _containerDI.Verify() (ServiceHost.cs:170) and a per-request AsyncScopedLifestyle scope (:315-319), so scoped services do not leak across requests.
• Correct stream framing on input. ReadExactAsync loops until all requested bytes arrive and treats a zero read as a closed connection (ServiceHost.cs:517-540); the length prefix is parsed with NumberStyles.Integer/InvariantCulture.
• Per-request log correlation. LoggingConector.BeginContexto stores a worker/request/type/client context in an AsyncLocal (LoggingConector.cs:13-20) and CrearContextoConector builds a unique id per request - exactly the correlation id the checklist (5) asks for.
• Safe XML loading. XmlResolver = null (XmlHelper.cs:23) and a TryParse contract that returns an error string instead of throwing.
• HSM reply validation. InterpretarRespuesta checks the declared length against the body and the CCC<cmd>00000000 header (HSMService.cs:211-227); GeneraClave re-checks the embedded key length (:140-158).
• Parameter-count validation before indexing in both the HSM and RSA routers (HSMService.cs:49, 54, 64, 310; RSAService.cs:193).
• Operator authentication precedes every mutating admin operation (5 of 5 call sites) and the result of the authentication is compared with EstatusRegreso.OK before any SOAP mutation.
• `RSAXmlBuilder` uses `XElement` for the two requests it builds (RSAXmlBuilder.cs:16-40), which escapes values correctly - the pattern the remaining templates should adopt (CHR-FR-14).
• Cancellation is honored on all socket reads/writes through CancellationToken, and the listener is stopped from the token registration (ServiceHost.cs:221).
• Constants and XML-doc comments exist for most public members (the constants file is large but intentionally centralised).
