CHR-FR-8 - Every RSA reply is rejected: `EsValidoAnalisXml` looks up `TRANSACTION_RESPONSE` on the document instead of on `SERVICE_RESPONSE` (four copies) [Blocker] Locations: SOAP\RSAAuthenticationService.cs:114, 123; RSASynchronizationService.cs:137, 146; RSATokenService.cs:140, 149; RSAAdminService.cs:609, 618 (same ~66-line method in each).
Code block (csharp)
loXMLElement = loXMLDoc["SERVICE_RESPONSE"];                 // first child element of the DOCUMENT
if (loXMLElement == null) { trnResCode = "9"; trnResMsg = "XML invalido"; return false; }
 
loXMLElement = loXMLDoc["TRANSACTION_RESPONSE"];             // again the DOCUMENT's children - not loXMLElement's
if (loXMLElement == null) { trnResCode = "9"; trnResMsg = "XML invalido"; return false; }
XmlNode's string indexer returns the first child element with that name. An XML document has exactly one root element, so the two document-level lookups can only both succeed if the reply had two roots, which is not well-formed XML. Reproduced on System.Xml.XmlDocument with a nested <SERVICE_RESPONSE><TRANSACTION_RESPONSE trnResCode="0" trnResMsg="Success">... reply: doc["SERVICE_RESPONSE"] found, doc["TRANSACTION_RESPONSE"] not found, doc["SERVICE_RESPONSE"]["TRANSACTION_RESPONSE"] found. So the method returns false with trnResCode = "9" for every well-formed reply. Effect as written: autentica always returns 4 (access denied, RSAAuthenticationService.cs:50-62); sincroniza1/sincroniza2 always return 9 (the token lookup fails first); ObtenerInformacionTokenAsync always returns Estatus = ErrorGeneral (RSATokenService.cs:51-55), so informacion_token and the second half of autentica can never succeed; every mutating admin operation is refused with 3 (operator credentials invalid) because the operator authentication that precedes it always fails - no SOAP mutation is executed today. This also means CHR-FR-9, 10 and 19 are currently masked: they surface the moment the parser is fixed, so CHR-FR-8 must not ship without them. The success branch also expects TOKEN_ADMIN_RESPONSE/STATUS for every operation, including doAuthentication, which is unverified. *Verify:* only a captured real reply can confirm the effect in production; if a flat reply is returned the logic must still be rewritten, because the current code cannot be reconciled with any valid document. The two files were added in the initial commit c9576c5 (2026-08-07); the history was not used to infer what the real reply looks like.
Recommended: one parser class, tested with a captured reply for each of the 11 operations used:
