If the configured LimiteConcurrencia is greater than 5 the loop waits for permits that do not exist and OnStop hangs until the SCM kills the process; if it is smaller, in-flight requests are not waited for. There is also no timeout, so one hung HSM/RSA call (up to 60-90 s) or stalled client holds the stop. _cts?.Dispose() runs in finally (:568) while in-flight handlers may still use the token. The configured value is read in one place and the semaphore capacity in another (CHR-FR-24). LimiteConcurrencia itself is unverified. Recommended: one source for the limit (semaphore capacity = configuration), drain by waiting for the tracked in-flight tasks with an upper bound and RequestAdditionalTime, then dispose the token source.
